          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_GUcURR": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Lab Grown Diamonds: Redefining Modern Luxury",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_4TbydN": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>For us, it comes down to a few things you can’t see in a photo. How a ring sits next to another band. How a necklace moves when you walk. How a pair of earrings becomes so familiar you forget they’re there—until someone else notices.<br/><br/>We make fine jewelry with lab-grown diamonds and solid gold. Not because it’s trendy, but because these materials let us focus on what actually matters: cut, proportion, weight, and the way every detail works together over time.<br/></p><h3>What are Lab Grown Diamonds?</h3><p>lab grown diamonds are 100% authentic diamonds created in controlled laboratory environments rather than being mined from the earth. By replicating the natural geological process of intense heat and pressure, these gemstones possess the identical chemical, physical, and optical properties of mined diamonds. </p><p>Think of a lab grown diamond as a modern marvel of science. Instead of forming over billions of years beneath the earth’s surface, they are created with precision using two advanced, industry-standard methods:</p><ul><li>CVD (Chemical Vapor Deposition): A high-tech process where carbon atoms are deposited onto a diamond \"seed\" inside a vacuum chamber, allowing the crystal to grow layer by layer.</li><li>HPHT (High Pressure, High Temperature): A method that subjects carbon to the extreme heat and crushing pressure found deep within the Earth’s mantle to form a rough diamond.</li></ul><p>Whether created via CVD or HPHT, the result is a real diamond that is indistinguishable from a mined stone, even under a professional jeweler’s loupe. At Lucenjuri, we provide the full brilliance of a genuine diamond, grown through modern innovation rather than traditional mining.</p><h3>Are Lab Grown Diamonds Real? Understanding Their Composition</h3><p>This is one of the most common questions we hear, and the answer is a definitive yes. In fact, the Federal Trade Commission (FTC) officially classifies lab-created diamonds as real diamonds, recognizing that they are chemically, physically, and optically identical to those found in the earth.</p><p>When you look at a Lucenjuri diamond, you are looking at a 100% genuine carbon crystal. These stones share the exact same internal crystal structure as mined diamonds, along with the legendary 10/10 hardness on the Mohs scale. This means they offer the same fire, brilliance, and enduring sparkle that has made diamonds the ultimate symbol of love for centuries.</p><h3>Lab Grown Diamonds vs. Earth-Mined: Key Differences & Similarities</h3><p>The true difference is not found in the diamond, but in the journey. While both lab grown and mined diamonds offer identical brilliance and durability, lab grown diamonds avoid the environmental and ethical challenges often tied to traditional mining. When you choose a Lucenjuri diamond, you are choosing a conflict-free, transparent origin with a significantly lighter environmental footprint.<br/><br/>Lab-grown and mined diamonds share the same physical properties—100% carbon composition, 10/10 hardness, and identical brilliance. However, they are worlds apart in origin and impact: lab diamonds are conflict-free, low-carbon, and minimally disruptive to land, whereas mined diamonds involve complex supply chains, heavy land displacement, and a high ecological footprint.</p><h3>Value and Savings: Why Lab Grown Diamonds Cost Less</h3><p>One of the most practical benefits of this modern innovation is its accessibility. Lab diamonds generally cost 30% to 50% less than mined diamonds of the same quality.</p><p>Why the price difference? It is not a difference in quality. Instead, it is a difference in the supply chain. Mined diamonds have a long, expensive journey from deep within the earth through a global network of middle men. Lab grown diamonds have a shorter, more efficient path.</p><p>At Ecglosty, we pass these supply chain savings directly to you. This means you have the freedom to choose a larger carat size, higher clarity, or superior cut. We are making fine diamond jewelry accessible across a wider range of budgets, while still investing in a piece designed to be cherished for a lifetime.</p><h3>Why Choose ECGLOSTY for Jewelry That Speaks Without Saying a Word?</h3><p>At ECGLOSTY, we quietly obsess over the things you can't see in a photo—how a ring sits next to another band, how a necklace moves when you walk, how a pair of earrings becomes so familiar you forget they're there. We craft every piece in solid gold with lab-grown diamonds, spending our time not on trends or marketing claims, but on the proportions and finishes that make jewelry feel like an extension of you, not an announcement.</p><p>We invite you to set aside the usual jewelry rules. No expensive status signals. No waiting for permission to wear something special. Just well-made, thoughtfully designed pieces that earn their place in your daily life.</p><p>Because in the end, luxury is simpler than it's often made to seem. It's not about owning more. It's about knowing what's worth keeping.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
