                    "accordion_row_jEewpz": {
                      "type": "_accordion-row",
                      "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
                      "settings": {
                        "heading": "Can a jeweler tell the difference between a lab grown and a mined diamond?",
                        "open_by_default": false,
                        "icon": "none",
                        "width": 20
                      },
                      "blocks": {
                        "text_xyKGHd": {
                          "type": "text",
                          "settings": {
                            "text": "<p>Not by sight alone. To the naked eye, or even under a jeweler’s loupe, lab grown and mined diamonds look exactly the same. Both are pure carbon crystals and display identical brilliance and fire. Only specialized laboratory equipment can detect the subtle growth patterns that indicate a diamond was grown in a lab.</p>",
                            "width": "100%",
                            "max_width": "none",
                            "alignment": "left",
                            "type_preset": "rte",
                            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
