                    },
                    "accordion_row_6nBCKR": {
                      "type": "_accordion-row",
                      "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
                      "settings": {
                        "heading": "What is the difference between CVD and HPHT growth methods?",
                        "open_by_default": false,
                        "icon": "none",
                        "width": 20
                      },
                      "blocks": {
                        "text_YritFp": {
                          "type": "text",
                          "settings": {
                            "text": "<p>Both are advanced, proven methods for growing high-quality diamonds. HPHT (High Pressure, High Temperature) recreates the extreme conditions found deep within the earth, while CVD (Chemical Vapor Deposition) grows diamonds layer by layer from a carbon-rich gas. Both methods produce diamonds that are identical in quality, beauty, and structure.</p>",
                            "width": "100%",
                            "max_width": "none",
                            "alignment": "left",
                            "type_preset": "rte",
                            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                            "font_size": "1rem",
                            "line_height": "normal",
                            "letter_spacing": "normal",
                            "case": "none",
                            "wrap": "pretty",
                            "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                            "background": false,
                            "background_color": "#00000026",
                            "corner_radius": 0,
                            "padding-block-start": 0,
                            "padding-block-end": 0,
                            "padding-inline-start": 0,
                            "padding-inline-end": 0
                          },
                          "blocks": {}
                        }
                      },
                      "block_order": [
                        "text_YritFp"
                      ]
                    },
                    "accordion_row_YhfkrE": {
                      "type": "_accordion-row",
                      "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
                      "settings": {
                        "heading": "Are lab grown diamonds considered ethical and sustainable?",
                        "open_by_default": false,
                        "icon": "none",
                        "width": 20
                      },
                      "blocks": {
                        "text_KnTdg4": {
                          "type": "text",
                          "settings": {
                            "text": "<p>Definitely. lab grown diamonds are widely considered a more ethical and sustainable alternative to traditional mining. Because they are created above ground, their production avoids the large-scale land disruption and complex ethical concerns often associated with diamond mining.</p>",
                            "width": "100%",
                            "max_width": "none",
                            "alignment": "left",
                            "type_preset": "rte",
                            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                            "font_size": "1rem",
                            "line_height": "normal",
                            "letter_spacing": "normal",
                            "case": "none",
                            "wrap": "pretty",
                            "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                            "background": false,
                            "background_color": "#00000026",
                            "corner_radius": 0,
                            "padding-block-start": 0,
                            "padding-block-end": 0,
                            "padding-inline-start": 0,
                            "padding-inline-end": 0
                          },
                          "blocks": {}
                        }
                      },
                      "block_order": [
                        "text_KnTdg4"
                      ]
                    },
                    "accordion_row_CCRRkw": {
                      "type": "_accordion-row",
                      "settings": {
                        "heading": "Do lab grown diamonds have flaws or inclusions?",
                        "open_by_default": false,
                        "icon": "none",
                        "width": 20
                      },
                      "blocks": {
                        "text_THg6Qj": {
                          "type": "text",
                          "settings": {
                            "text": "<p>They can, just like mined diamonds. Because lab grown diamonds form over time using natural carbon, internal inclusions or surface blemishes may occur during the growth process. These characteristics are graded using the same strict standards as mined stones. At Ecglosty, we carefully hand-select \"eye-clean\" diamonds only. This ensures that even if a diamond has a tiny inclusion visible under a microscope, it will have no visible flaws to the naked eye.</p>",
                            "width": "100%",
                            "max_width": "none",
                            "alignment": "left",
                            "type_preset": "rte",
                            "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                            "font_size": "1rem",
                            "line_height": "normal",
                            "letter_spacing": "normal",
                            "case": "none",
                            "wrap": "pretty",
